  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile avgpool with scvi_n200 is the strongest configuration so far (0.650 accuracy, 0.628 F1), multiprofile avgpool outperforms singleprofile and transformer aggregation for PCA, and image-only models are much weaker. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the scgpt RNA representation can improve over scvi_n200 under the same best profile and aggregation settings. This experiment tests that by changing only the RNA encoder to scgpt while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed. It is the best next use of budget because it exploits the strongest RNA-only direction, isolates the representation effect, and can either find a better encoder or confirm scvi_n200 before moving to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

